This crate is an original implementation for nv-rs of the role JohnnyGuitar NVSE plays for
mods (ADR-0016's "later built-ins"). It contains no code of the plugin and no decompiled code,
and none was read for it: it is written from public behaviour and documentation only.

Plugin: JohnnyGuitar NVSE (author carxt and contributors), release 5.25a is the target (the
owner's list had 5.20). Opcode block 0x3100. DLL file name johnnyguitar.dll as seen in the
owner's installation.

Sources used (2026-11-14): the plugin's repository page and README (https://github.com/carxt/
JohnnyGuitarNVSE: the GitHub API reports the licence as LGPL-2.1, the README says LGPLv2.1-only,
and points to its documentation on the GECK Wiki); xNVSE's documented plugin interface. The
GECK Wiki answered the fetch with HTTP 403 (a bot block); no workaround was attempted, so the
command documentation was not read. A command is built only from public names, parameter lists
and behaviour, with a note beside it of what it was built from.

Commands built (2026-11-20), from the Tale of Two Wastelands 3.4 scripts that call them (the
script text, SCTX, shows how each is called; the compiled bytes, SCDA, give its opcode) and the
engine's own data layouts only, no plugin code:
- IsDLLLoaded (string, optional int): built from the call `IsDLLLoaded "client"` expecting 0 and
  the command's name; it answers 1 when a plugin DLL of that name is in xNVSE's plugin list as
  nvse::plugins knows built-ins. The optional integer is accepted and ignored: its meaning is not
  in the sources read.
- InitExtraMiscStat (string), ModExtraMiscStat (string, int), GetExtraMiscStat (string): built
  from TTW's calls (Bobbleheads Found, Captives Rescued, Contracts Completed, ...): a table of
  named integers kept by the engine and saved in the co-save (nv-rs#405, a record of nv-rs's own).
- GetQuestFailed (alias GetQF; one quest): built from `if GetQuestFailed MS14 == 0` and the
  engine's quest layout (the failed bit TESQuest::SetFailed sets); also a condition function.
Opcodes (offset from 0x3100): each command sits at the opcode TTW's compiled scripts carry for it,
and the order of the names in the plugin's public registration list (JG/internal/JG/
JohnnyCommands.cpp of the repository above, LGPL-2.1; only the order and number of the names were
read, 412 on 2026-11-20, no function body) gives the same five opcodes: GetQuestFailed
0x3165, IsDLLLoaded 0x317E, GetExtraMiscStat 0x31E4, ModExtraMiscStat 0x31E5, InitExtraMiscStat
0x31EE. Other opcodes of the block stay empty.

The extra statistics are listed in the Stats menu after the game's own rows, by name. They are written to the co-save
in a record of type NVXS that nv-rs defines (the plugin's own record format is in no public
document read), so a real install's section is carried untouched and cannot collide. Not built: every other JohnnyGuitar command.

Licence check: LGPL-2.1-only. Because no code is copied, nothing of it is carried here; the
credit is given for the names and the behaviour this crate follows. The earlier translation of
its corrections of JIP's co-save is in crates/jip (see crates/jip/NOTICE).

Unverified: the plugin name handed to xNVSE (JohnnyGuitarNVSE) and the version number
(525): neither is stated in a public document read so far. They are inert while
ANSWERS_INSTALLED is false.
